# Whether a merge request is written for its reviewers: what, why, and
# whether the description matches the diff. One request, the state
# carries `mr` and `diff`.
# Format: https://github.com/chussenot/judgment/blob/main/docs/reference/jud-format.md
apiVersion: jud/v1
kind: Rubric
metadata:
  name: mr-hygiene
  minor: 4
  version: 1
  description: Whether a merge request explains what it changes and why, and matches its diff.
spec:
  questions:
    explains_what:
      type: noul
      instructions: Does `mr.description` say what the change does?
      criteria:
        true: a reader learns what behaviour, configuration or structure changes
        false: empty, a ticket key alone, or words that do not say what changes
    explains_why:
      type: noul
      instructions: Does `mr.description` say why the change is made?
      criteria:
        true: a reason, a problem solved, a request or a linked issue with its purpose stated
        false: no reason given, or only "as discussed"
    matches_diff:
      type: noul
      when: diff
      instructions: >-
        Do `mr.title` and `mr.description` describe the files and hunks in
        `diff.changed`, with nothing substantial in the diff left unmentioned?
      criteria:
        true: every substantial change in the diff is covered by the description
        false: the diff changes something the description does not mention, or the description claims a change the diff does not make
    breaking_flagged:
      type: noul
      when: diff
      instructions: >-
        If `diff.changed` removes or renames a public interface, a configuration
        key, an API field or a database column, does `mr.description` say so?
      criteria:
        true: no such removal in the diff, or the description flags it as breaking
        false: the diff removes or renames something others depend on and the description does not say so
  policy:
    explains_what:
      threshold: 0.6
    explains_why:
      threshold: 0.6
    matches_diff:
      threshold: 0.6
    breaking_flagged:
      threshold: 0.6
